1 DECK

   Makes the lines after it, in a command procedure, data for the image
   reading the procedure's input (SYS$INPUT), even those that start with
   "$".

   Format

     DECK

2 Description

   The data ends at an EOD command, or, with /DOLLARS, at a line
   starting with the string given; after that, any "$" line ends data
   again.  DECK comes after the command that runs the image, where its
   data begins.  An image reading the end line comes to its end of file
   there, and its next read gets the data after it.  DECK read as a
   command, with no image reading, is DCL-W-IVVALU.

2 Qualifiers
/DOLLARS[=string]

   Ends the data at a line starting with the string, 1 to 15
   characters, uppercased unless quoted, and matched case and all, in
   place of EOD.  Without a string, DCL's default end, EOD, is kept.

2 Examples

   1.$ TYPE SYS$INPUT
     $ DECK
     $ This line starts with a dollar sign, and is typed.
     $ EOD

     Types the line between DECK and EOD.

   2.$ RUN SORTER
     $ DECK/DOLLARS="*END*"
     $ banana
     *END*

     Gives SORTER its input, up to the line *END*.
